1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Weak acid questions give you different data, and

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,120
the data choose the method.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,960
A K a and a concentration?

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,080
Estimate x, then check it was fair.

5
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,440
A measured pH?

6
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:13,600
Work backwards to K a.

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,253
An ion that can give or take a

8
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,239
proton?

9
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,800
Compare its K a with its K b.

10
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:22,160
Here are four HSC-style questions.

11
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:24,480
Pause and try each one, then we'll work

12
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,400
it through, one step at a time.

13
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,480
Question one.

14
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:32,000
Hypochlorous acid is a weak acid that forms

15
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:34,160
when chlorine is added to pool water.

16
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,280
Calculate the pH of a zero point zero

17
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,320
five zero zero moles per litre solution at

18
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:43,200
twenty five degrees, given that K a is

19
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:45,360
three point zero times ten to the minus

20
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:45,760
eight.

21
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,800
Justify any approximation you make.

22
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,560
Pause here to answer.

23
00:01:00,967 --> 00:01:03,846
K a and a concentration, so set up

24
00:01:03,927 --> 00:01:06,886
the ICE table: the acid goes down by

25
00:01:07,047 --> 00:01:10,086
x, and each ion goes up by x.

26
00:01:10,407 --> 00:01:12,726
K a is tiny next to zero point

27
00:01:12,887 --> 00:01:15,766
zero five zero zero, so drop the x

28
00:01:15,847 --> 00:01:16,886
from the bottom.

29
00:01:17,007 --> 00:01:19,926
Then x squared is K a times c,

30
00:01:20,007 --> 00:01:21,846
one point five times ten to the minus

31
00:01:22,007 --> 00:01:24,726
nine, and x is three point nine times

32
00:01:24,807 --> 00:01:26,966
ten to the minus five moles per litre.

33
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:29,526
Now justify it.

34
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:32,486
x is only zero point zero seven seven

35
00:01:32,567 --> 00:01:36,166
percent of the concentration, far under five percent,

36
00:01:36,287 --> 00:01:37,966
so dropping x was fair.

37
00:01:38,247 --> 00:01:40,966
The pH is four point four one, two

38
00:01:41,127 --> 00:01:44,246
decimal places because x has two significant figures,

39
00:01:44,327 --> 00:01:45,126
from K a.

40
00:01:45,527 --> 00:01:47,846
And it's below seven, as an acid's should

41
00:01:47,927 --> 00:01:48,326
be.

42
00:01:49,534 --> 00:01:52,333
The classic mistake is forgetting the square root.

43
00:01:52,814 --> 00:01:55,293
Then x is one point five times ten

44
00:01:55,374 --> 00:01:57,853
to the minus nine, and the pH comes

45
00:01:57,974 --> 00:02:00,413
out at eight point eight two, a basic

46
00:02:00,494 --> 00:02:01,613
pH for an acid.

47
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:03,713
Question two.

48
00:02:04,274 --> 00:02:07,793
Chloroethanoic acid is a weak monoprotic acid with

49
00:02:07,874 --> 00:02:09,953
a K a of one point four times

50
00:02:10,034 --> 00:02:11,873
ten to the minus three at twenty five

51
00:02:12,034 --> 00:02:12,953
degrees.

52
00:02:13,314 --> 00:02:16,113
Show that the simplifying assumption can't be used

53
00:02:16,354 --> 00:02:18,593
for a zero point zero two zero zero

54
00:02:18,754 --> 00:02:20,473
moles per litre solution.

55
00:02:20,754 --> 00:02:22,793
Then calculate its pH.

56
00:02:23,074 --> 00:02:24,353
Pause here to answer.

57
00:02:34,767 --> 00:02:36,686
Try the shortcut first.

58
00:02:37,007 --> 00:02:39,806
x squared is K a times c, two

59
00:02:39,887 --> 00:02:42,366
point eight times ten to the minus five,

60
00:02:42,487 --> 00:02:44,926
so x is about five point three times

61
00:02:45,007 --> 00:02:46,366
ten to the minus three.

62
00:02:46,687 --> 00:02:49,366
Now check: that's twenty six percent of the

63
00:02:49,407 --> 00:02:51,886
concentration, far over five.

64
00:02:52,127 --> 00:02:54,686
About a quarter of the acid ionises, so

65
00:02:54,847 --> 00:02:57,566
c minus x is nowhere near c, and

66
00:02:57,647 --> 00:02:59,166
the shortcut doesn't hold.

67
00:02:59,567 --> 00:03:00,526
Keep the x.

68
00:03:01,734 --> 00:03:04,693
So K a equals x squared over zero

69
00:03:04,854 --> 00:03:08,093
point zero two zero zero minus x.

70
00:03:08,374 --> 00:03:10,853
Multiply both sides by the bottom, and gather

71
00:03:10,934 --> 00:03:14,213
everything on one side: x squared, plus K

72
00:03:14,294 --> 00:03:17,173
a times x, minus two point eight times

73
00:03:17,254 --> 00:03:20,053
ten to the minus five, equals zero.

74
00:03:20,094 --> 00:03:23,413
The quadratic formula, or your calculator's solver, gives

75
00:03:23,494 --> 00:03:26,373
one positive root: four point six times ten

76
00:03:26,454 --> 00:03:27,893
to the minus three.

77
00:03:27,974 --> 00:03:30,613
So the pH is two point three three.

78
00:03:31,834 --> 00:03:34,633
The classic mistake is keeping the shortcut answer

79
00:03:34,794 --> 00:03:36,313
after the check has failed.

80
00:03:36,794 --> 00:03:39,513
That gives two point two eight, about zero

81
00:03:39,674 --> 00:03:41,273
point zero five out.

82
00:03:41,594 --> 00:03:44,153
Once the check fails, the shortcut's answer goes

83
00:03:44,234 --> 00:03:44,713
too.

84
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:46,893
Question three.

85
00:03:47,374 --> 00:03:50,573
Benzoic acid is a weak monoprotic acid used

86
00:03:50,654 --> 00:03:51,933
as a food preservative.

87
00:03:52,494 --> 00:03:55,293
A zero point zero one five zero moles

88
00:03:55,374 --> 00:03:57,933
per litre solution of benzoic acid has a

89
00:03:57,974 --> 00:04:00,733
measured pH of three point zero three at

90
00:04:00,894 --> 00:04:02,493
twenty five degrees.

91
00:04:02,774 --> 00:04:04,973
Calculate K a and p K a for

92
00:04:05,094 --> 00:04:06,413
benzoic acid.

93
00:04:06,494 --> 00:04:07,853
Pause here to answer.

94
00:04:18,267 --> 00:04:20,906
This time the pH is given, so work

95
00:04:21,027 --> 00:04:21,706
backwards.

96
00:04:21,947 --> 00:04:24,186
The hydronium is ten to the minus three

97
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:27,626
point zero three, nine point three three times

98
00:04:27,707 --> 00:04:30,266
ten to the minus four moles per litre.

99
00:04:30,587 --> 00:04:33,706
Each ionised molecule makes one hydronium and one

100
00:04:33,787 --> 00:04:36,346
benzoate, so benzoate is the same.

101
00:04:36,907 --> 00:04:39,386
The acid left is zero point zero one

102
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:42,906
five zero minus that, zero point zero one

103
00:04:43,067 --> 00:04:43,706
four one.

104
00:04:44,934 --> 00:04:48,933
So K a is hydronium times benzoate, over

105
00:04:48,974 --> 00:04:51,653
the acid: nine point three three times ten

106
00:04:51,734 --> 00:04:54,613
to the minus four, squared, over zero point

107
00:04:54,774 --> 00:04:56,453
zero one four one.

108
00:04:56,534 --> 00:04:58,373
That's six point two times ten to the

109
00:04:58,454 --> 00:05:01,893
minus five, two significant figures from the pH's

110
00:05:01,974 --> 00:05:03,253
two decimal places.

111
00:05:03,494 --> 00:05:06,133
Then p K a is the negative log,

112
00:05:06,214 --> 00:05:07,413
four point two one.

113
00:05:08,634 --> 00:05:10,953
The classic mistake is writing the p K

114
00:05:11,114 --> 00:05:13,993
a as three point zero three, the same

115
00:05:14,074 --> 00:05:15,273
as the pH.

116
00:05:15,594 --> 00:05:19,193
The pH describes this solution, at this concentration.

117
00:05:19,674 --> 00:05:22,553
The p K a describes the acid itself.

118
00:05:23,767 --> 00:05:24,726
Question four.

119
00:05:25,287 --> 00:05:28,646
The hydrogen carbonate ion, from baking soda, and

120
00:05:28,687 --> 00:05:32,326
the dihydrogen phosphate ion, from a fertiliser salt,

121
00:05:32,407 --> 00:05:34,006
are both amphiprotic.

122
00:05:34,567 --> 00:05:37,126
Write an equation for each ion donating a

123
00:05:37,207 --> 00:05:40,006
proton to water and accepting one from it.

124
00:05:40,647 --> 00:05:42,806
Use the K a values to decide which

125
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:46,246
mainly happens, and predict whether each salt's solution

126
00:05:46,407 --> 00:05:48,166
is acidic or basic.

127
00:05:48,487 --> 00:05:49,846
Pause here to answer.

128
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:03,786
An amphiprotic ion runs two reactions with water,

129
00:06:03,867 --> 00:06:05,826
so compare their constants.

130
00:06:06,107 --> 00:06:09,786
For hydrogen carbonate donating, K a is given:

131
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:11,866
four point seven times ten to the minus

132
00:06:12,027 --> 00:06:12,506
eleven.

133
00:06:12,907 --> 00:06:16,826
Accepting, it becomes carbonic acid, its conjugate acid,

134
00:06:16,907 --> 00:06:19,226
so its K b is K w over

135
00:06:19,307 --> 00:06:22,506
carbonic acid's K a: two point three times

136
00:06:22,587 --> 00:06:23,986
ten to the minus eight.

137
00:06:24,267 --> 00:06:27,146
K b is about five hundred times bigger,

138
00:06:27,227 --> 00:06:30,266
so it mainly accepts a proton, making hydroxide.

139
00:06:30,747 --> 00:06:33,786
Sodium hydrogen carbonate solution is basic.

140
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,800
Dihydrogen phosphate is the other way round.

141
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:40,920
Donating, its K a is six point three

142
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,840
times ten to the minus eight.

143
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:46,520
Accepting, it becomes phosphoric acid, so its K

144
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,000
b is K w over seven point one

145
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,480
times ten to the minus three, just one

146
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:54,360
point four times ten to the minus twelve.

147
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:57,480
Now K a wins, so it mainly donates,

148
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,600
making hydronium.

149
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:02,360
Potassium dihydrogen phosphate solution is acidic.

150
00:07:03,567 --> 00:07:06,286
The classic mistake is finding K b from

151
00:07:06,327 --> 00:07:08,686
the ion's own K a.

152
00:07:08,767 --> 00:07:10,766
That gives one point six times ten to

153
00:07:10,807 --> 00:07:13,006
the minus seven, the K b of hydrogen

154
00:07:13,087 --> 00:07:16,126
phosphate, and the wrong answer, basic.

155
00:07:16,767 --> 00:07:19,166
K a times K b is K w

156
00:07:19,407 --> 00:07:22,046
only for a conjugate pair, so for an

157
00:07:22,127 --> 00:07:24,686
ion's K b, use the K a one

158
00:07:24,767 --> 00:07:25,646
proton up.

159
00:07:26,867 --> 00:07:29,106
So here's how to start any weak acid

160
00:07:29,187 --> 00:07:29,986
question.

161
00:07:30,307 --> 00:07:31,906
Read the data first.

162
00:07:32,147 --> 00:07:34,346
Given K a and a concentration?

163
00:07:34,547 --> 00:07:37,786
Estimate x, then check it's under five percent.

164
00:07:37,987 --> 00:07:40,386
If it isn't, solve the full equation.

165
00:07:40,627 --> 00:07:41,666
Given a pH?

166
00:07:41,827 --> 00:07:44,586
Work backwards, with no five percent check.

167
00:07:44,787 --> 00:07:46,306
Given an amphiprotic ion?

168
00:07:46,467 --> 00:07:48,666
Compare its K a with its K b,

169
00:07:48,787 --> 00:07:51,026
taken from the acid one proton up.

170
00:07:51,267 --> 00:07:53,746
Next, how a buffer resists a change in

171
00:07:53,827 --> 00:07:54,546
pH.

